# sshole-yocto lab sshd_config.
#
# Swapped in for the stock one through FILESEXTRAPATHS in the bbappend below:
# the stock openssh recipe's do_configure/do_install machinery copies
# ${UNPACKDIR}/sshd_config, and with this layer's files directory first on the
# search path the recipe installs THIS file without any other change. The
# recipe's sshd_hostkey_setup appends the enabled HostKey lines (ECDSA for the
# stock PACKAGECONFIG).
#
# PasswordAuthentication is on and PAM is explicitly off, so sshd
# authenticates through libc crypt() against /etc/shadow. On musl that is the
# CVE-2026-123158 condition; the glibc control image exercises the same
# non-PAM path with a different libc.

Port 22
ListenAddress 0.0.0.0
PasswordAuthentication yes
KbdInteractiveAuthentication no
PubkeyAuthentication no
PermitRootLogin prohibit-password
UsePAM no
AllowUsers alice bob
X11Forwarding no
PrintMotd no
PidFile /run/sshd.pid
LogLevel VERBOSE
Subsystem sftp internal-sftp
